  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Giolito brought a shutout into the ninth. That was enough.",
    "what_this_means": "A 2-0 win doesn't require much explanation when one pitcher doesn't allow a run through five innings. Lucas Giolito set the tone early. Four hits, no damage, two strikeouts. And the bullpen never let Oakland threaten after he left. Jeremiah Estrada, Adrian Morejon, Jason Adam, and Mason Miller combined for four scoreless frames with three strikeouts. The defense held. The pitching held. That's how this team wins when the bats don't carry the load. Ten strikeouts in the lineup tells you everything about the offensive night, but also why two runs felt like enough. Giolito's 2.70 ERA just dipped lower. The pen closed without drama. That margin is thin, but today it held.",
    "what_to_watch": "Luis Medina takes the mound tonight for Oakland with a 2.41 ERA. His own shutdown line so far this season. Michael King counters at 1:10 PM with a 2.23 ERA over his last four starts, and that matchup is the only story that matters in a pitching duel waiting to happen.",
